{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"childFocus"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"direction"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GtkDirectionType","preciseIdentifier":"c:@EA@GtkDirectionType"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direction"},{"type":"text","text":" argument indicates what kind of motion is taking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"place (up, down, left, right, tab forward, tab backward)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function calls the [vfunc"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.Widget.focus"},{"type":"text","text":"] virtual function;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"widgets can override the virtual function in order to implement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"appropriate focus behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"focus()"},{"type":"text","text":" virtual function for a widget should return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"true if moving in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direction"},{"type":"text","text":" left the focus on a focusable location"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside that widget, and false if moving in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direction"},{"type":"text","text":" moved the focus"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outside the widget. When returning true, widgets normally call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"